{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"agent_message","text":"I fixed the degraded service and submitted the mitigation once; the submission was accepted.\n\n**Root cause:** The `recommendation` Service had `internalTrafficPolicy: Local`, which was set alongside a recent `nodeSelector` pin to `kind-worker`. Its only endpoint was on `kind-worker`, but the frontend runs on `kind-worker2`. Calls from the frontend to recommendation were dropped and timed out, so `/api/recommendations` failed and the frontend degraded.\n\n**Fix:** I patched the Service to `internalTrafficPolicy: Cluster`. After that, recommendation calls from the frontend stopped timing out, and 10 sequential checks of the recommendations API and homepage all returned 200 in about 10–15 ms.\n\n**Not changed:**\n- The `nodeSelector` pin on `recommendation` (revision 2) and on `frontend` are still in place. They are not what broke traffic once the Service policy is `Cluster`, but they could cause scheduling issues if `kind-worker` goes down.\n- The `accounting` image is a `nightly` build, which is not pinned to a release. This is off the request path, so I left it alone."}}
